`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:["Pairing covers the whole workspace: after launch, people can tag Claude Tag in any channel it has joined. It joins the public channels you select at launch, if the Launch step lists any; after that, members bring it in one channel at a time, and it joins on its own only where an admin has set an auto-join channel-name rule (section 4). To keep it to channels you choose, for a pilot for example, see ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://claude.com/docs/claude-tag/admins/restrict-access#limit-claude-tag-to-specific-channels",children:"Limit Claude Tag to specific channels"}),". How members add it, and how those joins appear in Slack's audit log, is covered in ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://claude.com/docs/claude-tag/admins/for-slack-admins#where-claude-reads-and-posts",children:"What the Claude Slack app can access"}),"."]}),`
