`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h2,{id:"cost",children:"6. Cost aligns with the work Claude Tag does"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Channel work and group DM work bill to your organization's usage balance, and a spend limit caps how much of that balance Claude Tag can draw each month. One-to-one direct messages from someone who has connected a Claude account are the exception: they bill to that user's own seat, like the rest of their claude.ai usage."}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:["Someone in the workspace who hasn't connected a Claude account, other than a Slack guest, can DM Claude Tag one-to-one on your organization's balance for a limited time. That ends at whichever comes first: 7 days from their first such DM (or from starting the daily briefs Claude Tag offers them), $50 of usage (or your default limit for channels, if that's lower), or 50 sessions. After that, Claude Tag asks them to connect an account. The usage counts toward the organization-wide limit but doesn't show in the per-channel breakdown. Turning off ",(0,n.jsx)(r.code,{children:"Allow direct messages"}),", turning on the member-access restriction, or switching Claude Tag off for the workspace stops these DMs; see ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://claude.com/docs/claude-tag/admins/restrict-access#direct-messages-from-members-without-a-claude-account",children:"direct messages from members without a Claude account"}),"."]}),`
